Subject: [PATCH DRAFT] phy: qcom-qmp-ufs: track retained rail references

Track the load vote and enable reference independently for both QMP UFS
PHY rails when vdda-phy-always-on is present. The vdda-phy rail remains
enabled while idle with its load vote cleared; vdda-pll is load-zeroed
before its enable reference is released.

On any failed regulator transition, retain the corresponding software
state so a later power-on or final cleanup does not blindly acquire a
second enable reference. Preserve the original bulk path when the
property is absent. The special path fails closed unless the configured
list is exactly vdda-phy followed by vdda-pll.

This is an isolated AI1 candidate layered after the AI2 17-patch Stage A series.
It deliberately reuses the qmp_ufs_power_off() definition already supplied by
ROUND63; this patch must not add a second definition. It does not change the AI2
branch. Source/build validation is pending.

---
 drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-ufs.c | 351 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++----------------
 1 file changed, 216 insertions(+), 135 deletions(-)
